      "description": "Watch Queens Park Rangers vs Millwall highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The stage was set for a classic London derby as the Carabao Cup brought together two sides with everything to play for. On August 8, 2026 , the intensity was palpable from the first whistle as both teams looked to secure their passage to the next round in a match defined by tactical discipline and late-game heroics. A Cagey Opening at Loftus Road The Queens Park Rangers started with intent, looking to leverage the creative flair of Ilias Chair . Early in the match, Chair saw an effort blocked following a cross from Amadou Mbengue , signaling the home side's offensive ambitions. Millwall , however, remained resilient, absorbing pressure and looking for openings on the counter. Femi Azeez had a notable chance for the visitors in the 31st minute, but his left-footed effort missed the target. As the first half drew to a close, both defenses remained unbreached, leaving the match finely poised at 0-0. Second Half Breakthrough and Resurgence The deadlock was finally broken in the 53rd minute when Luke Cundle found himself in the right place at the right time. The Millwall attacker converted from very close range to give the visitors a precious lead. The QPR response was frantic; manager substitutions brought on Kwame Poku and Koki Saito to inject pace. Their persistence paid off in the 86th minute when a corner from Ilias Chair led to an own goal by Mark Sykes , leveling the scores at 1-1. The drama intensified in stoppage time as Lukas Jensen produced a vital save to deny Poku , ensuring the match headed to a shootout. Jensen’s Masterclass in the Shootout The penalty shootout turned into a showcase for Lukas Jensen , who delivered a performance for the ages. The Millwall goalkeeper saved four penalties in total, stopping efforts from Ilias Chair , Harvey Vale , Koki Saito , and Kwame Poku . While QPR goalkeeper Pierce Charles did his best to keep his side in it with saves against Camiel Neghli and Taïryk Arconte , it wasn't enough. Successful spot-kicks from Jake Cooper and a redeeming strike from Mark Sykes secured a 2-1 shootout victory for Millwall , capping off a night of pure footballing drama."
